.TH "KREUZER" "1" "" "kreuzer 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kreuzer \- income, expense and budget tracker for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]kreuzer\f[R] [\f[I]command\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]kreuzer\f[R] is a full\-screen terminal application for recording
income and expenses across several wallets, tracking category quotas and
a monthly budget, and visualising them with charts.
Data is stored as plain tab\-separated files, one per month.
.PP
Without a command it starts the interactive interface.
Press \f[B]?\f[R] inside it for the key list.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\f[B]export\f[R] [\f[I]YYYY\-MM\f[R]]
Print a month as CSV on standard output.
Defaults to the current month.
Expenses and outgoing transfers are negative.
.TP
\f[B]backup\f[R]
Write a timestamped \f[CR].tar.gz\f[R] of the data directory next to it
and print its path.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-dump\-keys\f[R]
Print the key bindings in effect, in configuration file syntax.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-check\f[R]
Verify required tools and show the configuration and data paths.
.TP
\f[B]\-V\f[R], \f[B]\-\-version\f[R]
Print the version.
.TP
\f[B]\-h\f[R], \f[B]\-\-help\f[R]
Print a short usage text.
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[I]\(ti/.config/kreuzer/kreuzer.conf\f[R]
Settings (\f[CR][general]\f[R]) and key bindings (\f[CR][keys]\f[R]).
Created on first run.
\f[CR]$XDG_CONFIG_HOME\f[R] is honoured.
.TP
\f[I]\(ti/Documents/kreuzer/\f[R]
Data directory, changeable with \f[CR]data_dir\f[R] in the
configuration.
Holds one \f[CR]YYYY\-MM.tsv\f[R] file per month, a \f[CR]meta/\f[R]
directory, and a lock file.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\f[B]NO_COLOR\f[R]
When set and non\-empty, colours are disabled and chart slices use
distinct glyphs.
.TP
\f[B]XDG_CONFIG_HOME\f[R]
Base directory for the configuration file.
.TP
\f[B]KREUZER_LIBDIR\f[R]
Override the library directory (development and tests).
.SH CONFIGURATION
The \f[CR][general]\f[R] section accepts \f[CR]data_dir\f[R],
\f[CR]currency\f[R], \f[CR]currency_pos\f[R] (\f[CR]prefix\f[R] or
\f[CR]suffix\f[R]), \f[CR]thousands\f[R], \f[CR]decimal\f[R],
\f[CR]pie_aspect\f[R] (terminal cell height divided by width, usually
2.0) and \f[CR]auto_purge_days\f[R] (0 disables).
The \f[CR][keys]\f[R] section maps each action to one or more
comma\-separated keys.
Two actions bound to the same key are rejected at startup.
.SH EXIT STATUS
\f[B]0\f[R] on success, \f[B]1\f[R] on an error such as a missing
dependency, an invalid configuration, or a data directory already in use
by another instance.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
bash 4.4 or newer, GNU awk, coreutils, util\-linux, findutils, grep and
tar.
A UTF\-8 terminal with truecolor support, at least 70 columns by 20
rows.
.SH SEE ALSO
The documentation in \f[I]/usr/share/doc/kreuzer\f[R] (architecture,
data format and key bindings).
